1️⃣ What is Resilience4j? ⚡

Resilience4j is a lightweight, fault-tolerance library for Java and Spring Boot designed to make microservices resilient to failures in distributed systems.

It provides modular components to handle common issues like service downtime, network glitches, and slow responses.

Key Features:
Feature	Description
Retry	Automatically retry failed calls a configurable number of times
Circuit Breaker	Stops calls to a failing service to prevent cascading failures
Rate Limiter	Limits the number of requests per unit of time
Bulkhead	Isolates failures to a single service or thread pool
Time Limiter	Times out slow-running requests
Why Resilience4j is Needed

In microservices, services often depend on other services. Without resilience patterns:

Service A → Service B → Service C

If Service B fails, it can cascade to Service A

Users may see errors or downtime

Network or temporary glitches cause unnecessary failures

Resilience4j solves this by:

Retrying failed calls

Blocking repeated calls to failing services

Returning fallback responses gracefully

Advantages over Hystrix

Lightweight (no heavy dependencies)

Modular (use only the patterns you need)

Supports functional and reactive programming

Fully compatible with Spring Boot

Real-World Example 🏦

In banking:

Payment Service calls an external fraud detection API

Network glitches or downtime may occur

Resilience4j ensures:

Retry if temporary failure

Circuit breaker if service is down for long

Fallback response to continue user experience

Payment Service → Fraud Detection API
     ↓ Retry / Circuit Breaker → Fallback
